    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Circle Touching Three Lines" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="16" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Open up a triangle: keep one side and let the other two be rays that don't have to meet. A circle still touches all three.\n\nAs in the inscribed circle, the dashed angle bisectors meet at the center, equally far from all three lines. The green perpendiculars show where the circle touches.\n\nDrag the yellow points. When the rays cross, this is the inscribed circle. Spread them apart and their lines cross on the other side: the circle touches that triangle from outside, as its excircle." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="64" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
  </Figures>
